Saturday morning is my favourite time.
I volunteer at the neighbourhood café every week.
When I arrive, Sunita didi is already there.
"Good morning, Maya!"
"Are you ready for today's rush?" she asks.
"Yes, Sunita didi, I am completely ready," I reply with a smile.
The café is really very crowded this morning.
Many local people come here to have breakfast.
I go behind the counter and start working.
A customer asks for coffee and a warm sandwich.
"Yes, brother, I will bring it right now," I say politely.
I quickly make fresh coffee.
Sunita didi takes the warm sandwiches out of the oven.
We both work together very fast.
Today a customer jokes with me, laughing.
I answer with a laugh too.
"Maya, give this plate to table number four," Sunita didi says.
I cheerfully serve the food to the customers.
The whole café fills with the smell of fresh coffee.
Sunita ji watches from afar, smiling.
